# NOT APPLIED - historical record only, do not add rules here.
#
# Vercel reads routing ONLY from `vercel.json` at the project root. This file
# was served publicly as a raw download (HTTP 200) while none of the rules
# below were in force - a file that looked like the route table and was not.
# The routes it used to carry now live in the root `vercel.json`:
#
#   * the four /<os>download routes -> the cubeon-downloads Worker
#     (GITHUB_TOKEN stays server-side; the repo is private, so anonymous
#     requests to GitHub Releases hit an auth wall, and signed asset URLs
#     expire within the hour)
#
#   * every page route needs NO rule at all. `cleanUrls: true` already serves
#     `help.html` at `/help`, `privacy.html` at `/privacy` and so on, which is
#     why the legal pages were removed from here on 2026-09-22.
#
# NEVER pair a `/page` -> `/page.html` redirect with `cleanUrls: true`: the
# host rewrites `/page.html` back to `/page`, so the pair loops forever with
# ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS. That shipped for /download, /help and /404.
